From 5589ad59b1e70c71bec2c7a61d68e17ff59ce6a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Riya Maheshwari <riyamaheshwri@google.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 09:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RESTRICT AUTOMERGE Fix projection redaction bypasses for
 location and OEM metadata in MediaProvider.

Implement robust projection sanitization and validation to prevent
bypasses of sensitive geolocation and OEM metadata column redactions
via SQL aggregate functions, repeated columns, and wildcard projections.

* Pre-validate projections early using the query builder compiler to
  block comma-separated projections and invalid space-containing
  aliases.
* Isolate SQL expressions from their aliases using a strict single-
  spaced ALIAS_PATTERN.
* Apply word-boundary regex (e.g., \blatitude\b) to detect sensitive
  columns even when wrapped inside aggregate functions.
* Redact sensitive columns as "null as alias" (preserving the original
  alias) to avoid breaking cursor column expectations in the caller.
* Expand explicit asterisk (*) wildcards in-place to ensure they undergo
  the same location and metadata redaction checks.
* Clone the static compatibility allowlist dynamically per-query to
  prevent memory leaks and side-effects.

SECURITY_PRESUBMIT_BYPASS_REASON=The comma-separated projection bypass
is completely blocked by early projection validation because
SQLiteQueryBuilder.setStrictColumns(true) is enabled for all non-system
callers. This causes the query to be rejected with an Invalid Column
exception before reaching the filter.

DISABLE_TOPIC_PROTECTOR

Bug: 484925508
Test: atest MediaProviderTests
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX

Change-Id: Iae687adceb85abbae48dcb7ce47e8d7badaa0630
